# Secrets. `.env.*` catches the copies an editor leaves behind - nano writes
# `.env.save` when it exits abnormally, and that file holds the same
# DASHBOARD_SECRET_KEY and POSTGRES_PASSWORD as the original. It was not
# ignored before, so it showed up as untracked, blocked deploy/update.sh's
# clean-tree check, and was one `git add .` away from being published.
# `.env.example` carries no real values and stays tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

.idea/
.vscode/

.DS_Store

# Everything under data/ is machine-generated at runtime (chrome profiles,
# screenshots, logs, per-account databases, test reports, GUI training
# captures) EXCEPT the product catalogue: that's sample fixture data that
# the dashboard's Products page and multiple tests read directly, so it must
# ship with the repo.
/data/*
!/data/products/

ai_models/
# Per-account configs and Chrome profiles are machine-specific
configs/accounts/

# TypeScript incremental build cache - regenerated every build, not source.
dashboard/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Extension signing key + packed artifacts (scripts/pack_extension.sh) -
# extension.pem is a private key and must never be committed; the .crx/xml
# are regenerated from extension/ + that key, also machine-specific (the
# update manifest embeds an absolute file:// path).
extension_build/


GIAI_THICH_CHI_TIET_AUTONOMOUS_AGENT.md

# Bản đồ mã nguồn sinh cục bộ (scripts/gen_code_map.py) - tham chiếu nội bộ, không commit
docs/CODE_MAP.md
